TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c08","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"the dictionary's tightest point: detector prime side = 2Cg*Re[windowed E_1(1/2,T0)] — D8's energy","checksum":"76bb3b99b32b96b174a93f9ff0c46066285f93c73d552836349e4f5fc1237877","id":"B1","limits":"dictionary only; convergence at sigma=1/2 is bought by the window","type":"B","x":"h = |H|^2 (test functions are squares)","y":"P = |Q|^2 (our autocorrelation family)"},{"buys":"W(f*f_tilde) computable numerically via prime powers; the bridge IS the formula equating termwise zero-side positivity with prime-side balance","checksum":"18e8a5e03a2f560f94c218a6bc42f13a1fbaedd19e019a69dbb7438f1fc8fcf4","id":"B2","limits":"translating is not proving — the positivity must come from the geometry independently (this is D8's move, but where the positivity IS RH)","type":"B","x":"the explicit formula's arithmetic side","y":"a prime-power sum (vertex towers, our native objects) minus archimedean terms"},{"checksum":"3517438c1ee89971eaf3ce6a56c35df86897c3b179657d010f91a2d8e3c9f0b8","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"Weil (1952) proved RH IS a positivity — W(f*f_tilde) >= 0 for all test f, where W is the explicit-formula distribution; over function fields, RH was proved BY a positivity with a known geometric source (intersection pairing on C×C)","note":"cited classical result (Bombieri 2000 exposition; Connes-Consani 2020), not re-derived in the text — hence the weaker label, per the native rules","status":"conjectural","type":"C"},{"checksum":"1377b8b2fc766f8d8e14885347db9e500549052be7e9fbecb17230749d1f78a1","id":"C2","kind":"claim","label":"Circularity warning: translating Weil is not proving RH — the positivity must come from the geometry independently","note":"methodological constraint governing 10a (literature warning)","status":"heuristic","type":"C"},{"checksum":"1e45a7bcb9200a95b39f9ef54740e755d52e0a5cc9fe8e94ef91135cea48edcd","id":"C3","kind":"question","label":"Granted the load limits (D9), what methodology / perspective / reference could construct the REST of the bridge — the hybrid span between geometric positivity (built, D1-D9) and the analysis that crosses Re(s) = 1?","note":"options 10a-10e considered systematically, in order, per the user; the pass completed 2026-09-30","status":"unstated","type":"C"},{"checksum":"d609d4c42cc1728f2f80b3e878e93691f60d9fe8604104bdf64afcc70ff00e00","generates":[{"prescription":"compute psi(x) via the truncated zero sum (explicit_formula.py)","stage":"implement the explicit formula"},{"prescription":"error falls 4.55 -> 1.36 as T goes 50 -> 400","stage":"compare against sieve-psi"}],"honest_boundary":"grounding only — zeros regulate the face-sum: E(x)=psi(x)-x is MADE OF zeros. No positivity claimed here.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D1","rule":"truncated zero sum reproduces sieve-psi's oscillations: error 4.55 -> 1.36 as T = 50 -> 400","subtitle":"Explicit formula grounded on the face-sum (10a-step1)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"truncated zero sum vs sieve-psi","expected":"error 4.55->1.36, T=50->400"}]},{"checksum":"4c4c05d69095c6106f03f6eb7dcc6a756872d78deaf8d66000a1c89b1233bb74","generates":[{"prescription":"check the symmetric formula zero-side vs prime-side to machine precision — fix prime-power ordering bugs en route (weil_positivity.py)","stage":"verify both sides"},{"prescription":"W(h) >= 0 exhibited with NO zeros used — pure prime-side","stage":"exhibit prime-side positivity"},{"prescription":"pole 2.266297 + archimedean -1.196347 - prime drain 1.069950 ~= 0 at a=0.5","stage":"decompose the balance"}],"honest_boundary":"prime-side positivity is CANCELLATORY, not termwise. Weil's criterion itself (positivity <=> RH) is cited, not derived — circularity warning: translating Weil is not proving RH; the positivity must come from the geometry independently.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D2","rule":"symmetric Guinand-Weil formula verified zero-side vs prime-side to machine precision (2e-16) for Gaussian squares h_a = |e^{-ar^2/2}|^2, a = 0.02/0.1/0.5; W(h) >= 0 exhibited with NO zeros — pure prime-side","subtitle":"Symmetric Guinand-Weil formula verified prime-side (10a-step2)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"zero-side vs prime-side agreement","expected":"2e-16 (machine precision)"}]},{"checksum":"a94229be87d079df072be0c66ad5cb356db25eb42b14608e48204eb8e0ad7de5","generates":[{"prescription":"sum of squares with an exact Fourier pair","stage":"build the detector"},{"prescription":"window with a zero inside (T0=50): oscillatory prime sum -0.59/-0.98; empty window (T0=100): +0.36, W all leakage","stage":"test windows"},{"prescription":"figure of merit = concentration (leakage 0.68 -> 0.30 -> 0.0007); price = uncertainty (1e-12 envelope at n=e^{7.4/w}: 41/1700/2.8e6) — Pareto frontier, no finite optimum","stage":"optimize"}],"honest_boundary":"pole = 0 for detectors, archimedean = positive background. TIGHTEST DICTIONARY (exact algebra): detector prime side = 2Cg*Re[windowed E_1(1/2,T0)] — our D8 energy; the window buys convergence at sigma=1/2.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D3","rule":"detector h_{T0,w} (sum of squares, exact Fourier pair): W(h) from primes alone agrees with the zero side to 4e-16 and counts zeros in a window, N+(B+) <= e^{1/2}W(h)","subtitle":"Prime-side zero detector (10a-step3)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"primes-only W(h) vs zero side","expected":"4e-16"},{"check":"window containing a zero (T0=50)","expected":"oscillatory prime sum -0.59/-0.98"},{"check":"empty window (T0=100)","expected":"+0.36, W all leakage"}]},{"checksum":"2aad74cd77ce538b8c536fa7a4a2640771a9165b4ad1bbee1476bfb4b9e6e46a","generates":[{"prescription":"M_{S,T} = 1/prod(S union T) — PD by sum-of-squares, Weil-shaped","stage":"form the quadratic"},{"prescription":"the constrained minimum is proved via (1-1)^{|S|}; the optimum is uniquely lambda* = mu","stage":"solve"},{"prescription":"the minimum recovers the Mertens product exactly; classical level-truncated 1/G(z) is the constrained (worse) version","stage":"recover delta(z)"}],"honest_boundary":"canonical template of an optimized face-quadratic form only — an upper-bound machine: PD by construction, no continuation, no zeros; parity barrier intact. The independent zero-detecting source is still open -> 10d.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D4","rule":"on Delta_z: min_{lambda_empty=1} sum_{S,T} lambda_S lambda_T / prod(S union T) = delta(z), uniquely attained at lambda* = mu","subtitle":"Selberg lambda^2 on the face complex: exact optimizer mu (10c)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"proved minimum value","expected":"delta(z), unique optimizer mu"},{"check":"numerical check","expected":"12 digits, z <= 19"}]},{"checksum":"9b7691bdeac88993225f7b0518179c8574ef78aef20ced81e0e309f10b32a311","generates":[{"prescription":"verify #E(F_{p^n}) = p^n + 1 - pi^n - pibar^n by direct counting on F_5, F_7 curves","stage":"count points"},{"prescription":"deg(1-/+phi) exhibited as point counts — PSD because degree counts","stage":"exhibit the PSD form"},{"prescription":"(i) Jacobian torus, (ii) Frobenius operator, (iii) counting-born PSD form, (iv) zeros as eigenvalues, (v) finite exact formula","stage":"read the template"}],"honest_boundary":"a TEMPLATE, exhibited not imported. Ledger: we HAVE counting positivity (Lambda>=0), finite PD face forms (10c), a windowed explicit formula (10a); we MISS the Jacobian-role space (Delta_infinity contractible), a Frobenius-like operator, and the pairing tying zeros to counting positivity. The missing object is operator-theoretic, not another inequality.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D5","rule":"finite EXACT explicit formula #E(F_{p^n}) = p^n + 1 - pi^n - pibar^n, verified by direct counting; RH = Hasse = discriminant <= 0 of the degree form Q(m,n) = p m^2 + a_p m n + n^2, PSD because degree counts","subtitle":"Function-field template on concrete elliptic curves (10d)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"point-count formula","expected":"exact, verified by direct counting"}]},{"checksum":"527def263024c7940885b28636852aa5e770e10ed1548a5617b5408de9094a55","id":"G1","result":"S_1 = 1+gamma/2-(1/2)log(4pi) is archimedean — no convergent prime-sum presentation possible (the proof uses only the functional equation); the Lambda-sums that want to be lambda_n's coefficients diverge as k!/eps^{k+1} (verified 7.45->156 across k,eps) — lambda_n needs their finite parts","title":"Li's criterion on the face-sum (10b)","transfer":"Weil is face-sum-native, Li is Dirichlet-native; Li is the sharp-cutoff (inadmissible) limit of Weil-type positivity. Lesson: the face-sum carries smoothed/windowed positivity, not coefficient positivity.","tried":"lambda_n >= 0 verified both ways (Keiper-Taylor exact, n<=40; zero-side reconciled via density-integral tail to 3 s.f.; caught+fixed own pairing bug)","type":"G","verdict":"CLOSED — Li's criterion does NOT live natively on the face-sum."},{"checksum":"81240cf6d031dcd1081207f49fe62c4d8bd06fb4bfea85c13fb58de296dca436","id":"G2","result":"w=0.5 -> 2.9e6 primes; w=0.25 -> 8.2e12 primes: infeasible — the prime-side detector's fundamental wall","title":"The prime-side detector's uncertainty wall (10e)","transfer":"zero-density audited as the unconditional-izer (plug-in point precise; estimates cited); 10d ledger unchanged","tried":"Montgomery-Vaughan mean value (1/2H)int|P|^2/S2 -> 1 (0.995->1.007); large sieve holds (ratios 0.004, 0.008); uncertainty cost curve quantified","type":"G","verdict":"CLOSED as a supporting tool — analytic amplifiers, not independent positivity sources."},{"checksum":"49c9438e86371e2fdd19e0ae8994aab3488b83b4e3a7201f89571cf860ad179c","from":"D2","id":"L1","rel":"supports","to":"V5","type":"L"},{"checksum":"f6762c35cf2ad34ee7d996cdfdf38f1cc05feb16eaaf786e28523b07e7c71e21","from":"G2","id":"L2","rel":"bounds","to":"D3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"68b066d1552a5b4d5afbef5b3448617eec1f4d866088d375ca43a98723f98b3d","from":"G1","id":"L3","rel":"refines","to":"B1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"4cb99057420eea39a9481c926994c721d8aa734aadaadd72c53530e4937b5fb8","consequence":"translation done: Weil positivity is face-sum-native (windowed/smoothed); detector built; optimization = Pareto frontier (no finite optimum). The open span (independent Gram/intersection source) belongs to the bridge program; 10d its natural home.","id":"V1","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"10a — Weil's criterion in the energy language","type":"V"},{"checksum":"b825bdeeed780afc9c23111db2abb2ab69d5fd195f19a106bc4b6ada226f78b2","consequence":"canonical template of an optimized face-quadratic form (exact optimizer mu, minimum delta(z)) — but an upper-bound machine: PD by construction, no continuation, no zeros; parity barrier intact. The independent zero-detecting source is still open -> 10d.","id":"V2","status":"exact","subject":"10c — Selberg's lambda^2 sieve on the complex","type":"V"},{"checksum":"122810b702d29900dd4097ee47552afc44c012d8f52ae6b3cbb6be9250c428a6","consequence":"template exhibited + ledger: the missing object is operator-theoretic (a 'Frobenius for Delta'), not another inequality. Toroidal question answered: plane for zeta's domain, torus (Jacobian) for the geometric explainer.","id":"V3","status":"exact","subject":"10d — function-field template","type":"V"},{"checksum":"0ad65c7df418c204c20392a9acfa80a2d89771ad2b5eac103da4541d66cda2d2","consequence":"verified on our objects; uncertainty wall quantified. Verdict: analytic amplifiers, not independent positivity sources; 10d ledger unchanged.","id":"V4","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"10e — analytic tools","type":"V"},{"checksum":"4b22c794f1597b9c13f33f200e01130f62d86ca315a38e7a82c1b19031607336","consequence":"systematic pass 10a-10e closed. The face-sum carries three verified positivity kinds (primitive counting Lambda>=0, Weil-type windowed, Selberg-type optimized); none detects zeros independently. Sharpest open question: the Frobenius-like operator (refines D4's).","id":"V5","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"Node 10 — the bridge program","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","B2":"B","C1":"C","C2":"C","C3":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D3":"D","D4":"D","D5":"D","G1":"G","G2":"G","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","V1":"V","V2":"V","V3":"V","V4":"V","V5":"V"},"wire_checksum":"a50125ffc2d5e02f42b40043e7f09593820d41cd43c1a88cc5fbc50831be227a"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1